    "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nThis PR refactors the ACE (RISC-V Cryptographic Extension) status tracking to provide finer-grained control over Cryptographic Register (CR) state management. The changes align the per-CR status tracking with the existing `sstatus.ACES` design pattern used for global ACE state.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Replaces single unprivileged read-only `acecrstatus` CSR with two privilege-specific CSRs: `sacecrstatus` (Supervisor) and `vsacecrstatus` (Hypervisor)\n- Updates CSR semantics to track Off/Initial/Clean/Dirty states per-CR, consistent with the `sstatus.ACES` model\n- Adds support for virtualized environments where `vsacecrstatus` substitutes for `sacecrstatus` when V=1\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/riscv/riscv-high-assurance-cryptography/new/main/.github/instructions?filename=*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
